-   from document content. Log light document frames, visibility/occlusion, gaps
-   and bounds changes. Three background probes are insufficient. A drop or
-   uncertain classification invalidates that trial; do not count it as PASS.
-5. Repeat ten **process** cold launches (not ten clicks or ten window reloads),
-   populate startup.json from raw observations, run the intake checker, then QA
-   reviews the recording. Restore app/display settings after the series.
-
-If a safe isolated prelaunch capture surface is unavailable, T020 stays BLOCKED.
-Do not modify production startup timing/visibility to help the recorder catch up.
-
-## T021 request-attempt procedure — observer selection remains a review decision
-
-Root fs_usage is not by itself a solution: syscall/socket visibility cannot prove
-absence of WebKit/CSP-blocked resource attempts. Do not request elevated capture
-until scope/coverage are established. The observer must cover both resource
-attempts and CSP violations, attribute app plus its owned WebKit processes, span
-all actions, and avoid unrelated application traffic.
-
-Evaluate WebKit Network inspection plus CSP violation instrumentation in the
-isolated QA host. WebKit states the Network table begins when Inspector opens;
-thus opening it after the journey is insufficient. Its URL breakpoints cover
-JavaScript APIs, not every possible native/subresource source. These are candidate
-components of an observer, not established complete production coverage.
-[WebKit Network](https://webkit.org/web-inspector/network-tab/),
-[WebKit URL breakpoints](https://webkit.org/web-inspector/url-breakpoints/).
-
-Before and after each journey, on a separate disposable calibration page/host,
-verify a known bundled resource request and a deliberate CSP-blocked request are
-both recorded with correct attribution. No external server is required; keep the
-blocked control blocked and do not relax production CSP. Separate calibration
-records from journey counts. Record gaps and process replacements explicitly.
-
-Run reading, theme changes, persistence/restart and blocked-content fixtures while
-the validated observer is active. Preserve raw events and process attribution;
-zero remote attempts may be reported only for that covered interval. A DOM image
-placeholder, empty socket list, or instrumented-only trace cannot close T021 on
-the production package. If the chosen mechanism requires enabling inspectability
-or injecting listeners, that evidence remains supplemental and the production
-coverage gap must be reviewed explicitly, not silently waived.
